<p>
  Hi <%= @user.display_login %>,
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3 tmp-mt-3">
  Your <%= Copilot.individual_product_name %> plan has ended and your account has now been transitioned to Copilot Free.
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  You can continue using Copilot Free at no cost. However, premium features and higher usage limits are no longer available on your current plan.
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3"><strong>Want to pick back up where you left off?</strong></p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  You can upgrade to a Copilot Pro or Pro+ monthly plan anytime to restore access to premium models, agentic features, and more.
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  &bull; Copilot Pro: $<%= Copilot::COPILOT_PRO_MONTHLY_BASE_PRICE %>/month (includes $<%= Copilot::COPILOT_PRO_MONTHLY_BASE_PRICE %> in monthly AI Credits and extra flex allotment)<br>
  &bull; Copilot Pro+: $<%= Copilot::COPILOT_PRO_PLUS_MONTHLY_BASE_PRICE %>/month (includes $<%= Copilot::COPILOT_PRO_PLUS_MONTHLY_BASE_PRICE %> in monthly AI Credits and extra flex allotment)
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3"><strong>Next steps</strong></p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  &bull; Upgrade or manage your plan: <%= link_to @settings_user_billing_path, @settings_user_billing_path %><br>
  &bull; Learn more about plan options: <%= link_to Copilot::COPILOT_FOR_INDIVIDUALS_BILLING_DOCUMENTATION, Copilot::COPILOT_FOR_INDIVIDUALS_BILLING_DOCUMENTATION %><br>
  &bull; Read the billing documentation: <%= link_to Copilot::COPILOT_BILLING_DOCUMENTATION, Copilot::COPILOT_BILLING_DOCUMENTATION %><br>
  &bull; Read the blog post: <%= link_to "GitHub Copilot is moving to usage-based billing", "https://github.blog/news-insights/company-news/github-copilot-is-moving-to-usage-based-billing/" %>
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  Thanks for being part of the Copilot community &mdash; we hope to see you back.
</p>

<p class="tmp-mb-3">
  The GitHub Team
</p>
